  <body>
   

    <div class="p-3 mb-2 bg-dark text-white">
      <h2
        class="display-5 fw-bold"
        style="text-align: center">
        About ChemAR
      </h2>
      <p class="text-center">
        <!-- <br /> -->
        The Chemical Augmented Reality Project is an innovative web application
        designed to provide users with an immersive experience by enabling the
        visualization of 3D molecular models through Augmented Reality (AR).
        Leveraging the AR.js library, this application adeptly detects markers
        and seamlessly presents captivating 3D models directly within the user's
        web browser. These dynamic models are generated from .mol files,
        meticulously designed to emulate the classic "ball and stick" molecular
        representation, ensuring both accuracy and familiarity for users
        engaging with chemical structures. <br /><br /><br />
      </p>
      <h2
        class="display-5 fw-bold"
        style=" text-align: center">
        Team Mission
      </h2>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm">
          <p class="text-center">
            The Chemical Augmented Reality Project has been established to
            enrich the academic journey of Dalhousie students. Our mission is to
            provide an unparalleled immersive experience by utilzing the ability
            of Augmented Reality (AR) to visualize intricate 3D molecular
            models. At the heart of the web application lies the AR.js library,
            a development technology that detects markers, enabling a
            captivating list of 3D models directly accessible through your web
            browser. Through our passion for science and technology, we
            introduce dynamic molecular models, generated from .mol files. The
            classic "ball and stick" representation is emulated, displaying both
            accuracy and familiarity for users engaging with complex chemical
            structures.<br /><br /><br />
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h2
        class="display-5 fw-bold"
        style=" text-align: center">
        Project Features
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-group text-center">
        
          <h4>Visualizations and 3D Models</h4>
          <p class="text-left">
            The Chemical Augmented Reality Project utilizes both the PubChem and
            ChemSpider Representational State Transfer - Application Programming
            Interface(s) (REST-APIs); which have access to an extensive
            repository of chemical data. These provide the .mol molecule files
            that display the structure of the molecular elements and compounds
            that are present on the web application.
          </p>
          <p>
            Read more about the PubChem API
            <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6030920/" target="_blank">here</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Read more about the ChemSpider API
            <a href="https://developer.rsc.org/" target="_blank">here</a>.
          </p>
        </li>
        
          <h4>Molecules</h4>
          <p class="text-left">
            The Molecule page contains the molecule catalog which feature the
            deployed chemical elements and compounds, organized for user
            convienience. Additionally, users may further share or access these
            to retrieve specific molecular visual data on alternative devices
            via the Quick Response (QR) Code.
          </p>
          <p>
            Read more about the molecule catalog
            <a href="https://chem-space.com/" target="_blank">here</a>.
          </p>
        </li>
        
          <h4>Scenes</h4>
          <p class="text-left">
            The Scenes page contains information and data on the molecular
            elements of the periodic table.
          </p>
        </li>
        
          <h4>Lessons</h4>
          <p class="text-left">
            The lessons page contains information on specific compound
            structures and concepts covered within the course material.
          </p>
        </li>
        
          <h4>Study Help</h4>
          <p class="text-left">
            For any help or questions related to the content presented within
            the web application, it is advised that students reach out to their
            teaching assistant(s) or course instructor.
          </p>
        </li>
        <br /><br />
      </ul>

      <h2
        class="display-5 fw-bold"
        style="text-align: center">
      Privacy Policy
      </h2>
      <br />
        <ul class="text-center">
          <li class="list-group-item bg-dark text-white">
            <h4>Statement</h4>
            <p>
              The ChemAR project is committed to protecting the
              privacy of its users. The following outlines our privacy policy and
              practices.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="list-group-item bg-dark text-white">
            <h4>Personal Information</h4>
            <p> We do not collect any personal information from our users.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="list-group-item bg-dark text-white">
            <h4>External Links</h4>
            <p>
              The ChemAR project website may contain links to other websites.
              The ChemAR project is not responsible for the privacy practices
              or the content of such websites.
            <p>
          </li>
        </ul>
    <br /><br />

      <h2
        class="display-5 fw-bold"
